# The outgoing shorthand is PennMUSH behavior. /reply is a SharpMUSH extension, covered by engine tests.
::case page.shorthand  omitted recipients reuse the last successful outgoing targets
::login alice Alice alicepass
::login bob Bob bobpass
::as alice
page Bob=Explicit initial page
page Bare followup
page =Equals followup
page/noeval [add(1,2)] literal
page/noeval =[add(1,2)] literal
page Bob=
page =After empty explicit message

::case page.group  preserve group ordering and successful-only target memory
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
::as alice
page Bob Wiz=Group initial
page Group followup
::as wiz
@set *Bob=HAVEN
::as alice
page Bob Wiz=Partial delivery
page Partial followup
::as wiz
@set *Bob=!HAVEN

::case page.reconnect  outgoing target memory is a character attribute across reconnect
::logout alice
::login alice Alice alicepass
page Reconnected followup

::case page.override  only the existing Pemit_All authority bypasses page refusals
::as wiz
@set *Bob=HAVEN
::as alice
page/override Bob=Unauthorized override
::as wiz
@set *Bob=!HAVEN
